The problem asks for the condition for a rank-n tensor field T to be totally anti-symmetric. This is a standard differential geometry / tensor calculus question. Let me answer it directly in the TUI without using any tools.

A rank-n tensor field T is totally anti-symmetric if it changes sign under the interchange of any two of its indices. Equivalently, for any permutation σ of {1,...,n}:

T^{i_σ(1)...i_σ(n)} = sgn(σ) T^{i_1...i_n}

Or in terms of swapping any two indices: T^{...i...j...} = -T^{...j...i...}

